10.1 Value anchors from public data
Water: Dhaka WASA loses about 60 crore litres per day. Recovering just 10% of that (6 crore litres, or 60,000 m³ per day) is worth about Tk 36.6 crore per year at the residential tariff of Tk 16.70, or about Tk 54.8 crore at a production cost of Tk 25 per 1,000 litres. Only the leakage share of the loss counts, so the achievable value is lower.
Gas: recovering 10% of the Tk 3,790 crore lost in FY2023-24 would be worth about Tk 379 crore, again only for the leakage share.
One pinhole: a 1 mm hole at about 100 kPa wastes about 214 m³ per year, worth only about Tk 3,570 at the residential tariff. The water case therefore rests on many leaks, avoided excavation, pressure and service reliability, not on a single hole.
